      Wainscoting Height Rules: The 1/3 Ratio vs 32-36" Standards
    </h1>

    <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-300 max-w-3xl mb-6 leading-relaxed">
      Wainscoting has adorned interior walls since the 14th century, originally designed to insulate stone castles and protect plaster walls from chair backs. Today, nailing the correct height is an exercise in classical proportion: splitting a wall incorrectly makes rooms feel stunted, while adherence to the 1/3 or 2/3 ratio elevates ceiling perception.
    </p>

    <!-- Key Metrics Grid -->
